# Leaks LeakSanitizer finds inside vendored code, and nowhere else.
#
# ext/ is not this project's code and is not held to this project's rules - see
# CLAUDE.md, which says the same thing about the warning set. A suppression here
# is a statement that the leak is SDL's to fix, not an excuse for one of ours:
# every entry names the vendored function it starts in, so a leak that merely
# passes through SDL on its way out of gearstick still reports.
#
# Use it with:  LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=cmake/lsan.supp
# The sanitized presets set it for ctest already.

# SDL keeps a per-thread error buffer, allocated the first time a thread calls
# SDL_SetError and freed when SDL cleans that thread up. Threads created inside
# an audio backend - PulseAudio's callback thread is the one that shows up here -
# are not threads SDL created, so it never gets to free theirs. Two allocations,
# once per process, and gone when the process is.
leak:SDL_GetErrBuf
leak:AddPulseAudioDevice
